  m_Name: 09_GLOSSARY
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NotebookSection
  number: 09
  title: GLOSSARY
  unlocked: 1
  entries:
  - title: Terms A to M
    tag: 0
    body: "<color=#ffe2a8><b>Amplitude</b></color>\nA number (\u03B1 or \u03B2) that
      determines measurement probabilities of a basis state.\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>Ancilla</b></color>\nA
      helper qubit used to record a check, so data qubits need not be measured.\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>Bit-flip
      error</b></color>\nAn error that swaps |0\u27E9 and |1\u27E9, modelled as an
      unintended X gate.\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>CNOT</b></color>\nTwo-qubit gate that
      flips the target only if the control is 1.\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>Data qubit</b></color>\nA
      qubit that carries the encoded information (q0, q1, q2).\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>Ket
      |\u27E9</b></color>\nNotation for a quantum state, such as |0\u27E9.\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>Logical
      bit</b></color>\nInformation encoded across several physical qubits, for example
      |0_L\u27E9 = |000\u27E9.\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>Measurement</b></color>\nObtaining
      a classical result from a quantum system."
    bench: 0
    qiskit: 
  - title: Terms P to X
    tag: 0
    body: "<color=#ffe2a8><b>Parity / XOR (\u2295)</b></color>\nTells whether two
      bits differ (1) or agree (0).\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>Qiskit / Qiskit Aer</b></color>\nA
      Python toolkit for building quantum circuits, and its local simulator.\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>Shot</b></color>\nOne
      run of a circuit ending in a measurement.\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>Superposition</b></color>\nA
      quantum state combining basis states, such as \u03B1|0\u27E9 + \u03B2|1\u27E9.\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>Syndrome</b></color>\nThe
      parity-check results used to locate an error.\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>Verification</b></color>\nA
      check that the corrected circuit gives the expected result.\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>X
      gate</b></color>\nThe gate that swaps |0\u27E9 and |1\u27E9."
    bench: 0
    qiskit: 
  guides:
  - label: Introduction to Qiskit
    url: https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/guides/tools-intro
  - label: Get started with Sampler
    url: https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/guides/get-started-with-sampler
